{
  "slug": "sf-pool6",
  "name": "How you pay attention",
  "questionnaire_type": "composable",
  "instructions": "People pay attention in two ways. In the sensing mode, you take in what is here through your senses (sounds, textures, light, your breath) without needing to do anything with it. In the doing mode, you use what you know to plan, solve, judge, fix or get something done. Both are useful. These questions ask how you move between them. In general, how much do you agree with each statement? There are no right or wrong answers.",
